2026-10-16 by a subagent; the Math. Comp. text itself was not opened:
- the largest least prime of a Goldbach partition found below 4e18 is p = 9781, at
  n = 3325581707333960528, found by Silvio Pardi;
- the largest prime gap below 4e18 is 1476, after the prime 1425172824437699411.
PROVED here, zero sorry: no prime p < 9781 has n - p prime, so p(n) is at least 9781; and
none of the 1475 numbers strictly between that prime and it plus 1476 is prime. Each
composite comes with a divisor found by Python and checked by the kernel.
The three primality inputs now use the Lucas certificates extracted into
PrattCertificates.lean by CODEX task72. The two maxima over the range stay cited.
The certificates were first proved in Pratt.lean in run 20261016T2003Z-5561. VERIFY U-0054, run
20261016T2204Z-20593: every figure MATCH against sweet.ua.pt; the 1476 gap was found by
Tomas Oliveira e Silva.
AI-written Lean code, Claude, 2026-10-16. Checked only by the Lean kernel.
Binary Goldbach is OPEN.
